From 9b4c914592b4f3bb11678012e6a0b5c2b60befda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:34:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] notch-search: Search apps from the notch

Plinius: a tap on the notch of the folded top bar (touch only, not on
the lock screen) opens a minimal app search right below the notch: a
black card joined to the notch by a stem as wide as the notch, with an
entry and up to six hits from GLib's desktop file index. A tap on a hit
starts the app, Enter starts the first one. A tap next to the card, on
the notch again or Escape closes the search, so does locking the
screen. A tap counts up to 32 px next to the notch; without a notch the
middle of the top bar takes its place. The key notch-search in
org.plinius.display (GNOME Settings) turns the search off.

The stem has no corners: it flows out of the screen's top edge and into
the card with concave curves (8 and 12 px), so notch, stem and card
read as one shape.
